# Line endings.
#
# This repository is written on Windows and runs on Linux. Most of the time git's autocrlf
# handles that invisibly, and the one place it does not is a shell script: bash on the host
# reads a trailing carriage return as part of the command and fails with things like
# `$'\r': command not found`, which sends you looking at the wrong thing entirely.
#
# scripts/host-deploy.sh installs the application. It is not a place to find that out.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
.cpanel.yml text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to normalise them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary
*.tar.gz binary
